ext": "Sub here to the Odd Lots newsletter. Everyday in your inbox. https://t.co/25c7dc92bu https://t.co/1sdf2uFWBA", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113704442344448270"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-23T18:40:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113702220411625840"], "id": "2113702220411625840", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 945, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Citigroup gets Beijing’s approval for wholly owned securities firm in China\nhttps://t.co/GHMhnVHugo", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2113702220411625840"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113698732084547584", "3_2113698752590454784", "3_2113698773020893184"]}, "author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-23T18:28:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113698997345177876"], "id": "2113698997345177876", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 249, "impression_count": 59366, "like_count": 378, "quote_count": 18, "reply_count": 31, "retweet_count": 37}, "text": "Some centrists fantasize that because all LLMs have the ideology of Ezra Klein, that we may be on the doorstep of a great political moderation.\n\nI wrote about a fascinating paper from @ahall_research and Sho Miyazaki that, to my mind, opens the door to a very different outcome. https://t.co/djboGYFQHZ", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113698997345177876"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113691881783873536"]}, "author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-23T18:00:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113691938289524997"], "id": "2113691938289524997", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1838, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "1/ We get the Q1 2026 business employment dynamics data next Wednesday.\n\nWe talk a lot about the \"frozen\", low turnover market, as measured by JOLTS &amp; similar data.\n\nBUT: turnover induced by establishment openings/closings is actually up relative to pre-pandemic. https://t.co/JLdh3EShEW", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2113691938289524997"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113686645857800193"]}, "author_id": "3039504459", "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:39:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113686648286327048"], "id": "2113686648286327048", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 829, "like_count": 25, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Researchers created a new material that traps and “pumps” sound waves between layers of slightly mismatched one-dimensional moiré lattices. This can allow signals to be routed without loss for communication and information processing.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/ULjofzZ6V5 https://t.co/UdfA5NbQlR", "url": "https://x.com/PhysRevLett/status/2113686648286327048"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113661860398379008"]}, "author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-10-23T16:00:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113661863082758520"], "id": "2113661863082758520", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10357, "like_count": 46, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "October preliminary S&amp;P Global US Composite PMI down to 56 vs. 55.5 est. &amp; 55.9 prior … selling prices remained elevated while demand was firm and employment expanded … continues to suggest firm GDP growth\n@SPGlobalPMI https://t.co/eFFsV4azp1", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2113661863082758520"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113661749085782016"]}, "author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-10-23T16:00:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113661752567374180"], "id": "2113661752567374180", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 9239, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "October Kansas City Fed Services Index up to +10 vs. +1 est. &amp; 0 prior … revenue much stronger at +16 vs. +6 prior; employment up to +2 vs. -10 prior; both selling and input prices still high but a bit softer relative to September https://t.co/2bEBXc16CW", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2113661752567374180"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:58:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113661376673481016"], "id": "2113661376673481016", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 9116, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Our latest #OnInvesting podcast episode has dropped, on which @CollinMartinCS and I examine Treasury yields’ sharp swings, what stubborn inflation could mean for Fed policy, and why bonds can still provide income and diversification even as rates remain elevated … we also dig", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2113661376673481016"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:57:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113661163389042958"], "id": "2113661163389042958", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 12308, "like_count": 92, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "About to go on @BloombergTV!", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113661163389042958"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:56:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113660862162763835"], "id": "2113660862162763835", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 3596, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113314564834275596", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Something I don’t get about the “in gold price terms” mannerisms… why not use S&amp;P 500 total returns instead https://t.co/z0vMDGLiwk", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2113660862162763835"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:50:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113659295514669300"], "id": "21136592